rule base noStep where

-- THE ONE COMMAND. `induction-on "v"` at the prompt, standing in the yield the
-- surface program left, proves `valueNoStepAuto` completely and commits it, so
-- the following `yield` carries the import on to the end.
--
-- BE HONEST ABOUT WHAT THIS IS. The navigation below is written in, not found:
-- `V-absCase1`, `V-absCase`, `V-absMethod` and `goal1` are addresses known
-- before the rule runs, and `s` is named in a fenced fragment. **It is a
-- transcript with one real search inside it**, and the real one is the
-- `case s of { }`: nothing here names `E-beta`, `E-app1` or `E-app2`, and
-- elaboration selects the split's arms and discharges each by no-confusion on
-- its own. That part is genuinely found.
--
-- A VERSION WHOSE MOVES ARE SEVERAL CLAUSES OF ONE RULE DOES SEARCH AND DOES
-- REACH ∎ — and it cannot be reached from a do-block or through a `yield`,
-- because a rule that backtracks fails on return. That is `~7grfx` in
-- .jalivert/REPORT.md, and it is why this rule is deliberately deterministic:
-- **nothing in it is a multi-clause call, so no choice point is ever built.**
induction-on : Name -> ()
rule induction-on n :- when focus-is-hole
  do t = resolve-name n
     ; induction-core t
     ; goto-named "V-absCase1"
     ; elaborate surface`case s of { }`
     ; goto-named "V-absCase"
     ; solve
     ; goto-named "V-absMethod"
     ; solve
     ; goto-named "goal1"
     ; solve

